# Salmon Temaki Bento Box

Based on [https://www.cookwell.com/recipe/salmon-temaki-bento-box](https://www.cookwell.com/recipe/salmon-temaki-bento-box) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251122152652/https://www.cookwell.com/recipe/salmon-temaki-bento-box))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Bento Box Components

- [ ] 160 g [salmon]{ ing="salmon" }
- [ ] 100 g [sushi rice]{ ing="sushi-rice" }
- [ ] 50 g [edamame]{ ing="edamame" }
- [ ] 3 [seaweed handroll sheets]{ ing="seaweed-handroll-sheets" } (nori)
- [ ] [Kewpie mayo]{ ing="kewpie-mayo" }
- [ ] [Sriracha]{ ing="sriracha" }
- [ ] [Black sesame seeds]{ ing="black-sesame-seeds" }
- [ ] [Salt]{ ing="salt" } to taste

### Pickled Carrots & Serranos

- [ ] 2-3 [carrots]{ ing="carrots" }, peeled and julienned
- [ ] 3 [serrano peppers]{ ing="serrano-peppers" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 100 g [water]{ ing="water" } (2 parts)
- [ ] 50 g [rice vinegar]{ ing="rice-vinegar" } (1 part)
- [ ] 50 g [white vinegar]{ ing="white-vinegar" } (1 part)
- [ ] [Salt]{ ing="salt" }, a sprinkle
- [ ] [MSG]{ ing="msg" }, a pinch

## Recipe

1. Prepare the [sushi rice]{ ing="sushi-rice" } according to package directions and let cool

1. While rice is cooking, prepare the pickled vegetables:

   1. Combine [water]{ ing="water" }, [rice vinegar]{ ing="rice-vinegar" }, [white vinegar]{ ing="white-vinegar" }, [salt]{ ing="salt" }, and [MSG]{ ing="msg" } in a bowl
   1. Add julienned [carrots]{ ing="carrots" } and sliced [serrano peppers]{ ing="serrano-peppers" }
   1. Let marinate for at least 15 minutes
1. Cook [edamame]{ ing="edamame" } according to package directions and season with salt
1. Prepare [salmon]{ ing="salmon" }:
1. If using raw salmon for sashimi, ensure it is sushi-grade and thinly slice
1. Smoked salmon also works well in temaki and adds a rich, smoky flavor
1. Alternatively, pan-sear or bake salmon (see [Salmon Baked with Asparagus](../seafood/salmon_baked_with_asparagus.html) for baking instructions) and let cool
1. Assemble the temaki (hand rolls):

   1. Place a [sheet]{ ing="seaweed-handroll-sheets" } of nori on your palm, shiny side down
   1. Add a small amount of rice to the left third of the nori
   1. Top with salmon, pickled vegetables, and a drizzle of [kewpie mayo]{ ing="kewpie-mayo" } and [sriracha]{ ing="sriracha" }
   1. Roll from the bottom left corner to form a cone shape
1. Garnish with [black sesame seeds]{ ing="black-sesame-seeds" }
1. Serve with edamame on the side

## Notes

- Temaki are best eaten immediately after rolling to keep the nori crispy
- For a complete bento box, add other components like cucumber slices, avocado, or Japanese pickles
